<section id="S14" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">14 </span>Computational Cost</h2>

<div id="S14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S13.T10" title="In SHAP Analysis ‣ 13 Features Importance ‣ verthinking Causes Hallucination:Tracing Confounder Propagation in Vision Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> shows that our method incurs only 36% additional computational cost in terms of inference time compared to the default greedy search method.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S14.F12" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.07619v1/svar_failures.png" id="S14.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:685/824;" width="685" height="824" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S14.F12.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12</span>: </span><span id="S14.F12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The above examples illustrates that SVAR fails to detect hallucinated objects when the attention values are active in the intermediate layers.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S15" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">15 </span>Confounder Propagation Examples</h2>

<div id="S15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <a href="#S15.F13" title="In 15 Confounder Propagation Examples ‣ verthinking Causes Hallucination:Tracing Confounder Propagation in Vision Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> shows some examples of confounding propagation in LLaVA-1.5.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S15.F13" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.07619v1/conf_examples.png" id="S15.F13.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:685/884;" width="685" height="884" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S15.F13.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 13</span>: </span><span id="S15.F13.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Some examples of confounding propagation in LLaVA-1.5.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S16" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">16 </span>Qualitative Results</h2>

<div id="S16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide qualitative examples in Fig. <a href="#S16.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ 16 Qualitative Results ‣ verthinking Causes Hallucination:Tracing Confounder Propagation in Vision Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>, <a href="#S16.F15" title="Figure 15 ‣ 16 Qualitative Results ‣ verthinking Causes Hallucination:Tracing Confounder Propagation in Vision Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, <a href="#S16.F16" title="Figure 16 ‣ 16 Qualitative Results ‣ verthinking Causes Hallucination:Tracing Confounder Propagation in Vision Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, <a href="#S16.F17" title="Figure 17 ‣ 16 Qualitative Results ‣ verthinking Causes Hallucination:Tracing Confounder Propagation in Vision Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>.</p>
